<title>BELGIUM: Brussels bourse to delist Clabecq shares.</title>
<headline>Brussels bourse to delist Clabecq shares.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brussels bourse said on Monday it plans to delist shares in bankrupt Belgian steel maker Forges de Clabecq SA.</p>
<p>&quot;We will officially delist the shares today or tomorrow,&quot; deputy bourse director Anne Vleminckx told Reuters.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have already suspended the share,&quot; Vleminckx said.</p>
<p>She added that if the share was not delisted on Monday it would be suspended until delisting on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A Belgian commercial court declared the loss-making company bankrupt on Friday and appointed four receivers to run the firm.</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6816</p>
</text>
